        "uuid": "9f34c5dc_6db776e5",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/ims/rcs/uce/eab/EabProvider.java",
        "patchSetId": 14
      },
      "lineNbr": 44,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349878
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-11T15:55:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, it 1:1  between the contact and common table. I separate common and contact into two different tables since we will have a service that listen contact provider changed and update the contact table, the columns of common table only update when someone tries to query the capabilities and save the capabilities into the db.\n\nI think there are two options: \nOption 1: Separate to two table\n- Pros:\n  - It\u0027s helpful to reduce NULL in contact table(If no one save the capability to EAB DB).\n  - If one day common and contact table is not 1:1, we don\u0027t need to touch the DB schema.\n\n- Cons:\n  - We need to query two times first for update/insert/delete. We need to query contact and \ncommon tables first and update the capabilities.\n\nOption2: Merge them into one table\n- Pros:\n  - More easier to query/update/insert/delete\n\n- Cons:\n  - Some NULL in contact table.\n\nI\u0027m OK for both, what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "0ae07261_516b6cab",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 44,
        "startChar": 39,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 72
      },
